Thirst is free to use, but it is not open source. This license says what you
may and may not do. Anything not expressly allowed below is reserved by the
author.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a. Run the unmodified Thirst plugin on any Minecraft server that you own or
      administer, free of charge. This includes servers that accept donations
      or sell ranks, cosmetics or other items; running the plugin on such a
      server is fine.
   b. Change the configuration files Thirst creates (such as config.yml) for
      your own server.
   c. Read the source code, and build it yourself, for your own use on your own
      server.
   d. Link to the Thirst GitHub repository and describe the plugin.
   e. Fork the GitHub repository only to propose changes back to this
      repository (a pull request), as GitHub's terms allow.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO, WITHOUT THE AUTHOR'S WRITTEN PERMISSION

   a. Copy, re-upload, mirror, or otherwise distribute Thirst (the plugin file,
      the source code, or any part of either) anywhere, including inside
      modpacks, server packs, installers, hosting-provider catalogs and
      download sites. Point people to the official GitHub repository instead.
   b. Publish modified versions, forks or derivative works of Thirst, or reuse
      its code or assets in another project.
   c. Sell, rent, sublicense or charge for the plugin itself. (Charging for
      access to a server that runs Thirst is allowed, as stated in 1a.)
   d. Remove or change copyright notices, or present Thirst or any part of it
      as your own work.

3. CONTRIBUTIONS

   If you send the author a change (for example a pull request), you give the
